<title>UK: Redland shares up on roofing deal.</title>
<headline>Redland shares up on roofing deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Redland Plc rose on Wednesday after the company said it would receive a cash payment of 220 million stg from the reorganisation and merger of its European roofing interests with those of German associate Braas.</p>
<p>The stock was up 5-1/2p at 428-1/2 by 0809 GMT.</p>
<p>Redland said it would use the payment to strengthen its aggregates operations and to invest in growth opportunities in developing markets.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
